WEBVTT

00:10:29.371 --> 00:10:33.329
When we feel anxious or uncertain,
we tend to hold our breath.

00:10:33.329 --> 00:10:35.579
We're scared about what's
going to happen next,

00:10:35.579 --> 00:10:37.996
and so we hold onto what's
happening right now,

00:10:38.037 --> 00:10:40.537
which prevents movement,
which keeps us stuck.

00:10:41.621 --> 00:10:44.621
Far from helping us,
holding our breath holds us back.

00:10:45.329 --> 00:10:46.954
So we stop.

00:10:46.996 --> 00:10:48.454
We breathe.

00:10:48.454 --> 00:10:50.537
And then we observe:

00:10:50.537 --> 00:10:52.454
What's happening around us?

00:10:53.162 --> 00:10:54.912
How do we feel about that?

00:10:55.621 --> 00:10:57.704
My friends Greg and Kanisha

00:10:57.746 --> 00:11:01.496
told me that I should watch the play
"Pipeline" by Dominique Morisseau.